I sit at the table and eat my dinner.
Bruno comes to me.
He sits right next to my chair.
He looks at me.
His eyes are very big and sad.
He wants to have my food.
I laugh, but I stay firm.
"No, Bruno," I say.
"You are not getting it."
He whines a little bit.
"Go into your basket!" I say strictly.
Bruno stands up slowly.
"You must stay in your basket."
He goes there and lies down.
I look at him.
"Dogs are not allowed to eat human food," I explain.
Bruno sighs quietly and closes his eyes.
I finish eating my dinner in peace.
